Original commit body from 847e816125071bca12cd422198a460e808868837:

--max-symbols containment (nodes(K1) subset-of nodes(K2)) was violated on
6 of 8 real bakeoff maps, deterministically. Three budget-dependent
mechanisms, all in the seed machinery the prior containment test never
exercised (entrypoints: [], force-include off):

1. The entrypoint cap switched regimes on len(eps) > max_symbols
   (1/3 vs 1/2), so growing the budget past the entrypoint count jumped
   the forced set discontinuously.
2. The cross-cutting seed budget (max//2 - len(forced)) SHRANK as the
   forced set grew - at a larger budget the cross-cutting seeds could
   vanish entirely (caddy 50->100 dropped its Dispenser dispatch
   endpoints and fmt.Errorf).
3. The coverage stop counted seed centrality, so a larger budget's bigger
   seed set inflated start coverage and stopped the centrality fill
   earlier.

Fix (default path only): ONE fixed-order seed list (entrypoints by
-confidence, then cross-cutting endpoints by -edge_count) under ONE
monotone quota (max//2; floor-of-one reserved for entrypoint seeds), plus
a budget-independent positional stop in select_by_coverage computed from
the global centrality order alone. A prefix of a fixed list under a
monotone quota is nested by construction. Connectivity mode keeps the old
adaptive policy - bridging is not a ranked prefix and containment was
never its contract.

Verified: real-map sweep 8/8 OK (was 2/8); TestSeededContainment pins the
property across budgets straddling the regime boundary at two coverage
targets, with feature-preservation guards. 226 compact + 207 CLI tests
green.

